Z||000000||Warren Harrell||04-17-2001||09:56 PM||||I would like to know the difficulty of swapping in a V8, Chevy or Caddy. I have a lot of knowledge on the Chevy small block,(I could probably build one in my sleep, but who cant their about as simple as it gets.)The caddy  I'm not to sure about. I have some experience in engine swapping. I installed a 350 in My little Chevy S10. I am sure there is alot more difficulty in a fiero swap though. Any info will be appreciated.||||reg||3
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-17-2001||10:52 PM||||Depending on how hard you want to make your life, you can get the V8 kit from Archie  for the install of a 350GM engine or build a kit yourself.  If I have read the stuff on engine swaps, the wiring maybe the most challenge, once you have the kit.  Do a search on V8's or go to the vendor list at the bottom of the page to go to Archies web site for information.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Tryxalon||04-17-2001||10:53 PM||||If you put the 350 in the S-10, swapping a SBC into a Fiero "ain't no big thing", <P>HOWEVER! -- <BR> You do need a couple of specific parts:  <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/v8fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/v8fiero.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||6
